---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="An independent exploration of useful ideas. Discover what Truth to Live By stands for and how we approach evidence, interpretation and everyday life."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">WHY WE’RE HERE</span>
      <h1>
        Understanding is a beginning.
        <br />
        <em>Living is the point.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Truth to Live By is an independent home for useful ideas from philosophy, psychology,
        relationships and human performance.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>
        We are interested in what an idea means when it leaves the page. How it changes a
        conversation. What it asks of an ordinary afternoon. Whether it helps us see ourselves or
        one another more clearly.
      </p>
      <div class="about-statement">
        “What is the truth here that somebody could actually live by?”
      </div>
      <p>
        That is our central editorial question. We approach it with curiosity, care and a
        willingness to change our minds.
      </p>
      <h2>Good questions. Careful thinking.</h2>
      <p>
        A compelling story is not automatically good evidence. A respected thinker can be insightful
        in one area and mistaken in another. We aim to distinguish what someone claims, what the
        available evidence suggests, and our own practical interpretation.
      </p>
      <ol class="method-list">
        <li>
          <span>
            <strong>Discover.</strong> Begin with an idea or question worth exploring.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>
            <strong>Investigate.</strong> Seek the source and understand what it actually says.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>
            <strong>Contextualise.</strong> Ask where the idea applies, and where it may not.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>
            <strong>Challenge.</strong> Look for limitations, counterarguments and uncertainty.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>
            <strong>Synthesise.</strong> Bring the useful parts into a clear, honest account.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>
            <strong>Apply.</strong> Offer a practical reflection without promising more than we
            know.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Three connected areas of life.</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/ideas/topic/self/">Self</a> explores attention, identity, meaning and resilience.{' '}
        <a href="/ideas/topic/relationships/">Relationships</a> considers communication, friendship
        and human connection. <a href="/ideas/topic/living-well/">Living Well</a> looks at the
        practices and conditions of everyday life.
      </p>
      <h2>One brand. Different ways in.</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href={brand.youtube}>YouTube channel</a> explores ideas on screen.{' '}
        <a href={brand.instagram}>Instagram</a>, <a href={brand.tiktok}>TikTok</a> and{' '}
        <a href={brand.facebook}>Facebook</a> offer shorter encounters. This website gives those
        ideas a lasting home, with room for context, references and further reading.{' '}
        <a href="/join/">One Truth to Live By</a> will bring a considered idea into your inbox.
      </p>
      <h2>Transparent about how we work.</h2>
      <p>
        AI tools may assist research, production and presentation. Synthetic presenters, where used,
        should be clearly identified; they are not real experts. The brand remains responsible for
        its published material, and AI output is not a substitute for verifying a source.
      </p>
      <p>
        Health and science coverage should make uncertainty visible and link to appropriate
        evidence. Practical interpretations are not individual medical, psychological, legal or
        financial advice.
      </p>
      <h2>Open to correction.</h2>
      <p>
        Ideas deserve scrutiny, including ours. Substantive changes should carry an updated date
        and, where appropriate, a correction note. If something needs attention,{' '}
        <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Newsletter />
  </div>
</Base>
